   <indicator measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">1.1. The government endorsed and submitted the Senate Bill on Budget Modernization which institutionalizes the Cash Budgeting System to promote fiscal discipline in the budget preparation, execution, and monitoring processes. (DBM)</narrative>
    </title>
   </indicator>
   <indicator measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">1.2. The government enacted Republic Act No. 11966 on Public-Private Partnership (PPP) Code of the Philippines to: (i) integrate climate resilience, sustainability, and gender and development policies into PPP projects; (ii) uphold high standards of environmental and social safeguards; (iii) enhance bankability of PPP projects for private partners to provide a credible pipeline of projects; and (iv) ensure efficient risk allocation between the government and the private sector. (PPP Center)</narrative>
    </title>
   </indicator>
   <indicator measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">1.3. The government approved Executive Order No. 29 to modernize public financial management (PFM) processes through the Integrated Financial Management Information System (IFMIS), to harmonize key PFM functions including budget management, budget execution, cash management, and accounting and reporting. (DBM)</narrative>
    </title>
   </indicator>
   <indicator measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">1.4. The government approved Executive Order No. 31 to institutionalize the Open Government Partnership, an international platform of the national and local governments, and civil society organizations, to promote transparency and citizens participation in government processes through citizen access to budgetary data, thereby strengthening social accountability and empowering citizens. (DBM)</narrative>
    </title>
   </indicator>
   <indicator measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">1.5. The government adopted the National Asset Management Plan (NAMP) which mandates the government agencies to digitalize asset records and implement the Asset Management System (AMS) to improve accountability, sustainability, and financial efficiency of government assets. (DBM)</narrative>
    </title>
   </indicator>
   <indicator measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">11 Dec 2024 | News Release: https://www.adb.org/news/adb-help-boost-efficiency-public-funds-philippines</narrative>
    </title>
   </indicator>
